er to adverse reactions to certain foods that do not involve the immune system, distinguishing them from food allergies. These intolerances are often linked to enzyme deficiencies, such as lactose intolerance, where the body lacks the necessary enzymes to properly digest specific foods. The reactions associated with food intolerances are non-immune and can lead to various symptoms, particularly gastrointestinal issues, as well as other health problems. In summary, INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS are characterized by their non-IgE mediated nature, resulting in a range of adverse effects without the involvement of the immune response.", "URTICARIA:Urticaria is a skin reaction characterized by hives, often associated with allergic responses to food.", "ANAFLAXIA ALÉRGICA ORAL:Anafilaxia alérgica oral is a severe allergic reaction that occurs after the ingestion of certain foods.", "BRONCOESPASMO:Broncoespasmo is a condition characterized by the tightening of the muscles around the airways, which can be triggered by food allergies.", "RINITIS:Rinitis is an inflammation of the nasal mucous membrane, which can be caused by food allergies.", "ANGIOEDEMA:Angioedema is a condition involving swelling beneath the skin, often related to allergic reactions to food.", "ENTEROCOLITIS INDUCIDA POR PROTEÍNAS DE LA DIETA:Enterocolitis inducida por proteínas de la dieta is a gastrointestinal condition triggered by dietary proteins, often seen in food allergies.", "TOXINAS BACTERIANAS:Toxinas bacterianas are harmful substances produced by bacteria that can cause adverse reactions to food.", "SOCIETY OF ALLERGOLOGY AND CLINICAL IMMUNOLOGY:The Society of Allergology and Clinical Immunology (SEAIC) is an organization that conducts epidemiological studies on allergies and intolerances in Spain.", "ALLERGIES:Allergies are adverse reactions to certain foods that can affect 1-3% of the global population, with higher prevalence in children.", "GLUTEN INTOLERANCE:Gluten intolerance affects about 1% of the general population and is a type of food intolerance.", "GENETIC PREDISPOSITION:Genetic predisposition refers to the inherited likelihood of developing food allergies, influenced by environmental factors.", "IGÉ:IgE es un anticuerpo que juega un papel crucial en las reacciones alérgicas, siendo secretado por el sistema inmune en respuesta a alérgenos alimentarios.", "CELULAS DE LANGERHANS:Las células de Langerhans son células del sistema inmunológico que captan alérgenos a través de la barrera cutánea y son importantes en la respuesta alérgica.", "LINFOCITOS TH2:Los linfocitos TH2 son un tipo de célula T que se activan en respuesta a alérgenos y son responsables de la producción de IgE."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}